# TrackID local development environment.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and adjust values as needed. `.env` is gitignored;
# `.env.example` is the documented reference. scripts/start_dev.sh sources `.env`
# when present, and the Go command-line tools load it via the `internal/env`
# package (from the repo root).
#
# Every value below matches the defaults already used by docker-compose.yml and
# the scripts, so a plain `cp .env.example .env` gives a working stack.

# --- API server (cmd/trackid) -------------------------------------------------
# development (the default) turns off a feature whose settings are missing or whose service is
# down; production stops instead (docs/deployment.md, "Production mode").
# TRACKID_ENV=development
# Addresses or CIDR ranges whose X-Forwarded-For gives the client's address; empty trusts none.
# TRUSTED_PROXIES=
# Every secret below may instead be read from a file: <NAME>_FILE=/path (docs/deployment.md).
PORT=8082
DATABASE_URL=postgres://trackid:trackid_dev@localhost:55432/trackid?sslmode=disable
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:56379/0
JWT_SECRET=local-development-secret
# Optional. When set, new accounts get "<username>@<EMAIL_DOMAIN>"; when
# empty, their email is just the username.
EMAIL_DOMAIN=
# Optional. Microsoft Teams messages (docs/follow-plan.md): each user may set a Power Automate
# webhook on their profile and get each notification there too. SECRETS_KEY encrypts the webhooks
# (32 bytes, base64 or hex: `openssl rand -base64 32`); empty turns Teams off. Changing it makes
# the stored webhooks unreadable. APP_URL is the frontend's address, which the message's button
# opens. TEAMS_WEBHOOK_HOSTS limits where webhooks may point (comma-separated host suffixes;
# empty means Power Automate's and Office 365's). TEAMS_LANGUAGE is pt-BR (default) or en.
SECRETS_KEY=
APP_URL=http://localhost:8082
# TEAMS_WEBHOOK_HOSTS=.logic.azure.com,.powerplatform.com,.webhook.office.com
# TEAMS_LANGUAGE=pt-BR
# Optional. The base map's raster tiles, served to the frontend by /api/config: a URL template
# ({z}/{x}/{y}) and its credit as HTML. Empty means OpenStreetMap's public tiles.
# MAP_TILE_URL=
# MAP_TILE_ATTRIBUTION=
# Optional. Override where the server looks for the built frontend (defaults to
# frontend/dist under the repo root).
# TRACKID_WEB_DIST=frontend/dist

# --- Object storage: SeaweedFS's S3 gateway (docker-compose.yml) ------------
# Also read by scripts/backup_data.sh / restore_data.sh.
S3_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:59000
S3_ACCESS_KEY=trackid
S3_SECRET_KEY=trackid_dev_storage
S3_BUCKET=trackid-local

# --- Vision: face detection + embedding ---------------------------------------
# github.com/rodfileto/trackid-vision. The API uses it for face detection on
# evidence (POST .../detect-faces); cmd/worker uses it for
# embedding.TaskTypeComputeCodification. Left empty, both log a warning and run
# without it rather than failing to start -- see its README for where to get
# the ONNX weights and onnxruntime build. See README "Models and licences":
# the SCRFD detector is non-commercial research only.
#
# Which detector VISION_DETECTOR_PATH holds: "yunet" (default, MIT) or "scrfd".
# Embeddings from the two are not comparable -- re-embed after switching.
VISION_DETECTOR=yunet
VISION_DETECTOR_PATH=
VISION_RECOGNIZER_PATH=
# Optional; trackid-vision has its own default.
VISION_SHARED_LIBRARY_PATH=
# Optional. "true" to use the CUDA execution provider; falls back to CPU if
# unavailable.
VISION_USE_GPU=false
# Only used when VISION_USE_GPU=true: a directory containing the CUDA/cuDNN
# runtime libraries libonnxruntime_providers_cuda.so needs at load time
# (libcudart/libcublas/libcublasLt/libcudnn*/libcufft/libcurand/libnvrtc).
# Without a full system CUDA toolkit install, these can be pulled from PyPI's
# nvidia-*-cu12 wheels (each is just a zip -- no pip/sudo needed) and their
# lib/*.so* files copied into one directory. IMPORTANT: this must be set in
# the actual shell environment before the Go binary execs -- glibc's dynamic
# linker reads LD_LIBRARY_PATH once at process start, so setting it via
# godotenv from inside the program (like every other var here) is too late.
# `set -a; source .env; set +a` before `go run ...` (as start_dev.sh and
# scripts/*.sh already do) works; `go run ...` on its own does not.
LD_LIBRARY_PATH=

# --- Fingerprint: SourceAFIS extraction + matching -----------------------------
# sourceafis-sidecar/, run as its own docker-compose service. Used by
# cmd/worker for fingerprint:extract_codification/fingerprint:extract_identity_feature/
# fingerprint:sync (the fingerprint package). Left empty, fingerprint tasks
# aren't processed -- fingerprint enrollments/lifts are still stored, just
# without a template or a SYSTEM match. Matches the docker-compose host port.
FINGERPRINT_SIDECAR_URL=http://localhost:58090

# --- Worker ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# How many tasks cmd/worker runs at once. Optional; 10 when unset.
# WORKER_CONCURRENCY=10

# --- Reports: WordCraft (docs/facial-reports-plan.md) ---------------------------
# wordcraft-cli renders an issued report's PDF with the engine the editor runs, so it breaks
# pages where the examiner saw them break; left empty, reports can be drafted but not issued.
# The web build (apps/wordcraft-web, `trunk build --release`) is the in-app editor, served by the
# API at /wordcraft/ on the app's own origin; left empty, the editor is not available.
WORDCRAFT_CLI=
WORDCRAFT_WEB_DIR=

# --- Geocoder: addresses <-> coordinates for locations ------------------------
# Addresses are looked up first in IBGE's census address list, loaded into the
# database (scripts/load_cnefe.sh <UF>), then in a Nominatim (OpenStreetMap)
# server, then as the municipality (docs/geocoding-plan.md). Empty GEOCODER_URL
# means no Nominatim: the census list and the municipalities still work.
# GEOCODER_URL=public uses OpenStreetMap's own instance
# (https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org), which then receives the addresses
# searched and the points clicked that the census list can't answer; its usage
# policy allows at most 1 request/s, requires an identifying User-Agent, and
# forbids autocomplete and bulk geocoding (importers refuse it). Results are
# OpenStreetMap data (ODbL): any map or list showing them must credit
# "© OpenStreetMap contributors".
GEOCODER_URL=
GEOCODER_USER_AGENT=trackid (+https://github.com/rodfileto/trackid)
# Optional contact address sent with each request (the policy asks for one for
# heavier use).
GEOCODER_EMAIL=
# Optional Go duration between requests; empty = 1s on the public instance, none
# on another.
GEOCODER_MIN_INTERVAL=

# --- Assist: a local model drafting registrations (assist package) -------------
# A language model runs locally and drafts a request/occurrence/case from a request's files,
# for a coordinator to review. ASSIST_ENDPOINT is the OpenAI-compatible base URL of a local
# server such as Strata or Ollama; ASSIST_MODEL names the model. Both empty means drafting is
# disabled and the worker logs a warning rather than failing to start. Nothing is sent to an
# outside service.
# ASSIST_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1
# ASSIST_MODEL=qwen3.8-flash-next
# ASSIST_API_KEY is sent as a Bearer token, for a server that requires one (Strata does; Ollama
# does not). Leave it empty when the server needs none.
# ASSIST_API_KEY=
# ASSIST_TIMEOUT bounds one draft, as a Go duration; empty means 5m. A local model writing a few
# dozen tokens a second can take minutes on a long request.
# ASSIST_TIMEOUT=5m

# --- AI mode: analysts asking the data in plain language (ask package) ---------
# Any server speaking the OpenAI chat protocol with tool calling, local or not: ASK_ENDPOINT is the
# base URL (the client appends /chat/completions), ASK_MODEL names the model and ASK_API_KEY is sent
# as a Bearer token when set. With neither endpoint nor model set the AI mode uses the ASSIST_*
# settings above, and with those unset too it is off. See docs/ask-plan.md.
#
# A server outside the institute only ever reads synthetic data: the question is refused, and nothing
# is sent, while any occurrence or case description doesn't start with SIMULATED. A loopback or private
# address, or a host name with no dots, counts as inside; any other host as outside.
#
# ASK_EXTRA_BODY is a JSON object of request fields the server wants, since servers differ on what
# they require or reject. Keep the single quotes.
#
# A local server (Strata, Ollama):
# ASK_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1
# ASK_MODEL=qwen3.8-flash-next
# ASK_API_KEY=
# ASK_EXTRA_BODY='{"temperature":0,"chat_template_kwargs":{"enable_thinking":false}}'
#
# Claude, through Anthropic's OpenAI-compatible endpoint (an outside server, so synthetic data only):
# ASK_ENDPOINT=https://api.anthropic.com/v1
# ASK_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
# ASK_API_KEY=
# ASK_EXTRA_BODY='{"max_tokens":16000}'
#
# ASK_TIMEOUT bounds one question, all its turns together, as a Go duration; empty means 5m.
# ASK_TIMEOUT=5m
